    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0404" n="336" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg336"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2353½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">17 January, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: This draft has my entire
                    approval. I hope that you will send it to the Governments you have indicated to
                    me; and I most sincerely hope that they will feel that we are right in our
                    argument and suggestion and will be willing to cooperate with us in attaining
                    the object we have in view, an object which they must surely wish to accomplish
                    as earnestly as we do, and which this seems in the circumstances the only
                    feasible way of reaching.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
